        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Tobacco's detrimental effects on calcium metabolism\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tobacco consumption is linked to negative health outcomes, particularly concerning bone health. Smoking is a known risk factor for osteoporosis, and avoiding tobacco is crucial for individuals requiring calcium supplementation. The relationship between tobacco use and calcium absorption highlights the importance of public health initiatives aimed at reducing smoking rates to improve overall health outcomes [Data: Reports (614); Entities (1291); Relationships (509)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Fortified foods as a strategy to combat calcium deficiency\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Fortified foods are designed to enhance dietary calcium intake, particularly in at-risk populations. These foods are enriched with essential nutrients, including calcium and iron, to address common deficiencies. The fortification of foods is a public health strategy aimed at improving nutritional status and preventing health complications associated with inadequate calcium intake [Data: Reports (614); Entities (11513); Relationships (8275)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Dairy products as primary calcium sources\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Dairy products are recognized as a primary source of calcium, essential for bone health, especially in children. They contribute significantly to meeting the recommended calcium intake levels. However, the consumption of dairy must be balanced with considerations of saturated fat content, particularly in certain diets. The relationship between dairy intake and calcium levels is critical for maintaining strong bones and preventing osteoporosis [Data: Reports (614); Entities (7333); Relationships (8252)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Calcium's relationship with vitamin D\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Calcium and vitamin D are interdependent nutrients that play crucial roles in bone health. Vitamin D enhances calcium absorption in the intestines, making it essential for individuals with calcium deficiencies. This synergistic relationship is particularly important for elderly patients and those with conditions affecting nutrient absorption, such as celiac disease. Ensuring adequate levels of both nutrients is vital for preventing osteoporosis and other bone-related health issues [Data: Reports (614); Relationships (8237)].\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Calcium's role in preventing rickets\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Rickets is a condition caused by calcium deficiency, particularly in children, leading to weakened and deformed bones. The condition can also arise from malabsorption issues, emphasizing the need for adequate calcium intake in vulnerable populations. Preventing rickets through proper dietary management and supplementation is crucial for ensuring healthy bone development in children [Data: Reports (614); Entities (5683); Relationships (8249)].\"\n        }\n    ]\n}", "input": "\nYou are an AI assistant that helps a human analyst to perform general information discovery. Information discovery is the process of identifying and assessing relevant information associated with certain entities (e.g., organizations and individuals) within a network.\n\n# Goal\nWrite a comprehensive report of a community, given a list of entities that belong to the community as well as their relationships and optional associated claims. The report will be used to inform decision-makers about information associated with the community and their potential impact. The content of this report includes an overview of the community's key entities, their legal compliance, technical capabilities, reputation, and noteworthy claims.\n\n# Report Structure\n\nThe report should include the following sections:\n\n- TITLE: community's name that represents its key entities - title should be short but specific. When possible, include representative named entities in the title.\n- SUMMARY: An executive summary of the community's overall structure, how its entities are related to each other, and significant information associated with its entities.\n- IMPACT SEVERITY RATING: a float score between 0-10 that represents the severity of IMPACT posed by entities within the community.  IMPACT is the scored importance of a community.\n- RATING EXPLANATION: Give a single sentence explanation of the IMPACT severity rating.\n- DETAILED FINDINGS: A list of 5-10 key insights about the community. Each insight should have a short summary followed by multiple paragraphs of explanatory text grounded according to the grounding rules below. Be comprehensive.\n\nReturn output as a well-formed JSON-formatted string with the following format:\n    {{\n        \"title\": <report_title>,\n        \"summary\": <executive_summary>,\n        \"rating\": <impact_severity_rating>,\n        \"rating_explanation\": <rating_explanation>,\n        \"findings\": [\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_1_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_1_explanation>\n            }},\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_2_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_2_explanation>\n            }}\n        ]\n    }}\n\n# Grounding Rules\n\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids); <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X is the owner of Company Y and subject to many allegations of wrongdoing [Data: Reports (1), Entities (5, 7); Relationships (23); Claims (7, 2, 34, 64, 46, +more)].\"\n\nwhere 1, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, 46, and 64 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nDo not include information where the supporting evidence for it is not provided.\n\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nText:\n\nEntities\n\nid,entity,description\n5,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n6,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is an organization that is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n\nRelationships\n\nid,source,target,description\n37,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n38,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n39,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,The Unity March is taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n40,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,TRIBUNE SPOTLIGHT,Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity march taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n41,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,BAILEY ASADI,Bailey Asadi is speaking at Verdant Oasis Plaza about the march\n43,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,UNITY MARCH,Harmony Assembly is organizing the Unity March\n\nOutput:\n{{\n    \"title\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza and Unity March\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community revolves around the Verdant Oasis Plaza, which is the location of the Unity March. The plaza has relationships with the Harmony Assembly, Unity March, and Tribune Spotlight, all of which are associated with the march event.\",\n    \"rating\": 5.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderate due to the potential for unrest or conflict during the Unity March.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza as the central location\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza is the central entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza's association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n----Reports-----\ncommunity,full_content\r\n614,\"# Calcium and Nutritional Health Community\n\nThe Calcium and Nutritional Health Community focuses on the essential mineral calcium and its relationships with dietary components and health conditions. Key entities include Vitamin D, dietary fiber, tobacco, fortified foods, and dairy products, all of which play significant roles in calcium metabolism and overall health.\n\n## Calcium's essential role in bone health\n\nCalcium is a vital mineral essential for maintaining bone health and preventing diseases such as osteoporosis. Adequate calcium intake is crucial, especially for vulnerable populations like the elderly and children. The recommended daily intake varies, but guidelines suggest between 1000-1500 mg for most adults. Calcium's importance is underscored by its inclusion in parenteral nutrition solutions for patients unable to consume adequate nutrition orally, highlighting its necessity for metabolic health and bone development [Data: Reports (1996); Entities (1996); Relationships (8239)].\n\n## The impact of dietary fiber on calcium absorption\n\nDietary fiber plays a significant role in digestive health and can influence calcium metabolism. High fiber diets are associated with improved overall health, particularly in the elderly and children. However, fiber can inhibit the absorption of certain nutrients, including calcium, which emphasizes the need for a balanced intake of both fiber and calcium-rich foods to ensure optimal health outcomes [Data: Reports (1996); Entities (4827); Relationships (8253)].\n\n## Tobacco's detrimental effects on calcium metabolism\n\nTobacco consumption is linked to negative health outcomes, particularly concerning bone health. Smoking is a known risk factor for osteoporosis, and avoiding tobacco is crucial for individuals requiring calcium supplementation. The relationship between tobacco use and calcium absorption highlights the importance of public health initiatives aimed at reducing smoking rates to improve overall health outcomes [Data: Reports (1996); Entities (1291); Relationships (509)].\n\n## Fortified foods as a strategy to combat calcium deficiency\n\nFortified foods are designed to enhance dietary calcium intake, particularly in at-risk populations. These foods are enriched with essential nutrients, including calcium and iron, to address common deficiencies. The fortification of foods is a public health strategy aimed at improving nutritional status and preventing health complications associated with inadequate calcium intake [Data: Reports (1996); Entities (11513); Relationships (8275)].\n\n## Dairy products as primary calcium sources\n\nDairy products are recognized as a primary source of calcium, essential for bone health, especially in children. They contribute significantly to meeting the recommended calcium intake levels. However, the consumption of dairy must be balanced with considerations of saturated fat content, particularly in certain diets. The relationship between dairy intake and calcium levels is critical for maintaining strong bones and preventing osteoporosis [Data: Reports (1996); Entities (7333); Relationships (8252)].\n\n## Calcium's relationship with vitamin D\n\nCalcium and vitamin D are interdependent nutrients that play crucial roles in bone health. Vitamin D enhances calcium absorption in the intestines, making it essential for individuals with calcium deficiencies. This synergistic relationship is particularly important for elderly patients and those with conditions affecting nutrient absorption, such as celiac disease. Ensuring adequate levels of both nutrients is vital for preventing osteoporosis and other bone-related health issues [Data: Reports (1996); Relationships (8237)].\n\n## Calcium's role in preventing rickets\n\nRickets is a condition caused by calcium deficiency, particularly in children, leading to weakened and deformed bones. The condition can also arise from malabsorption issues, emphasizing the need for adequate calcium intake in vulnerable populations. Preventing rickets through proper dietary management and supplementation is crucial for ensuring healthy bone development in children [Data: Reports (1996); Entities (5683); Relationships (8249)].\"\r\n618,\"# Calcium Disorders Community: Hypercalcemia and Hypocalcemia\n\nThe community focuses on calcium-related medical conditions, particularly hypercalcemia and hypocalcemia, which are characterized by abnormal calcium levels in the blood. Key entities include various medical conditions, hormones, and dietary strategies that are interrelated and impact patient health significantly.\n\n## Hypercalcemia as a critical health condition\n\nHypercalcemia is a medical condition characterized by elevated calcium levels in the blood, which can lead to serious health complications such as kidney dysfunction and increased risk of osteoporosis. It is often associated with conditions like hyperparathyroidism and certain malignancies, making it a significant concern in medical practice. The management of hypercalcemia typically requires medical intervention to lower calcium levels and mitigate associated health risks [Data: Entities (3639, 11941); Relationships (12064, 12058, 12025)].\n\n## Hypocalcemia and its implications\n\nHypocalcemia is defined by low calcium levels in the blood and can lead to various health issues, including muscle spasms and complications in patients with conditions such as pancreatitis. It is commonly observed in hospitalized patients and can be exacerbated by factors like vitamin D deficiency. Understanding the causes and management of hypocalcemia is crucial for patient care, particularly in vulnerable populations [Data: Entities (3640, 8404); Relationships (1058, 8406, 12068)].\n\n## The role of parathyroid hormone (PTH)\n\nPTH is a vital hormone that regulates calcium and phosphorus levels in the body. It plays a significant role in maintaining calcium homeostasis, and its levels can be influenced by various conditions, including vitamin D deficiency and parathyroid dysfunction. An imbalance in PTH can lead to either hypercalcemia or hypocalcemia, highlighting its importance in the pathophysiology of calcium disorders [Data: Entities (5525); Relationships (12058, 8381)].\n\n## Calcitonin's therapeutic role\n\nCalcitonin is a hormone that helps regulate calcium levels by inhibiting bone resorption and promoting renal calcium excretion. It is utilized in the treatment of conditions such as osteoporosis and severe hypercalcemia. The effectiveness of calcitonin in managing these conditions is still debated, but it remains an important therapeutic option in specific clinical scenarios [Data: Entities (4720); Relationships (12053, 10996)].\n\n## Dietary management of calcium disorders\n\nA controlled calcium diet is essential for managing both hypercalcemia and hypocalcemia. This dietary strategy focuses on regulating calcium intake to prevent and treat conditions such as osteoporosis and hypercalcemia. By carefully monitoring calcium consumption, individuals can support their bone health and prevent complications associated with abnormal calcium levels [Data: Entities (11470, 11472); Relationships (12060, 11040)].\n\n## Electrolyte disorders and their connection to calcium levels\n\nElectrolyte disorders, including hypercalcemia and hypocalcemia, can disrupt the balance of electrolytes in the body, affecting various physiological functions. Understanding the interplay between calcium levels and other electrolytes is crucial for effective patient management, particularly in cases of metabolic dysfunction [Data: Entities (3641, 11948); Relationships (12051, 12066)].\"\r\n621,\"# Maternal Health and Nutritional Dynamics\n\nThe community focuses on the interrelated health and nutritional aspects of mothers, fetuses, and conditions like hypocalcemia and insulin resistance. Key entities include mothers, various vitamin D metabolites, and conditions affecting maternal and fetal health, highlighting the complex interplay of nutrition, metabolism, and health outcomes.\n\n## The crucial role of mothers in fetal development\n\nMothers play a vital role in the health and development of their fetuses, providing essential nutrients and oxygen during pregnancy. This relationship is fundamental, as the mother's health directly influences fetal growth and development. For instance, mothers are responsible for ensuring adequate calcium levels, which are crucial for fetal skeletal development, and they also face various health challenges that can affect this process, such as insulin resistance and nutritional deficiencies [Data: Entities (2610, 5544); Relationships (10348, 10354, 10351)].\n\n## Impact of hypocalcemia on maternal and fetal health\n\nHypocalcemia, characterized by low calcium levels, poses significant risks for both mothers and their newborns. In mothers, it can lead to complications during pregnancy, while in fetuses, it can affect skeletal development. The relationship between calcium levels and hypocalcemia is particularly critical in newborns, as they are at risk for this condition due to inadequate calcium reserves. Therefore, maintaining proper calcium levels through dietary management and supplementation is essential for preventing hypocalcemia and ensuring healthy outcomes [Data: Entities (2738, 5541); Relationships (8241, 10598)].\n\n## The role of vitamin D metabolites in calcium metabolism\n\nVitamin D metabolites, such as calcitriol and colecalciferol, are crucial for calcium metabolism and play a significant role in preventing and treating hypocalcemia. Calcitriol enhances calcium absorption in the intestines, which is particularly important for mothers and newborns at risk of calcium deficiency. The interplay between these metabolites and calcium levels underscores the importance of adequate vitamin D intake during pregnancy to support both maternal and fetal health [Data: Entities (3479, 2253, 5690); Relationships (8285, 9441, 10341)].\n\n## Insulin resistance and its implications during pregnancy\n\nInsulin resistance is a common condition that can increase during pregnancy, affecting the mother's metabolism and potentially leading to complications such as gestational diabetes. This condition can also influence the mother's nutritional status and energy metabolism, impacting fetal development. Understanding the dynamics of insulin resistance is crucial for managing maternal health and ensuring optimal outcomes for both mothers and their babies [Data: Entities (5544, 5542); Relationships (10351, 1352)].\n\n## Nutritional strategies to manage electrolyte imbalances\n\nNutritional strategies, such as a potassium-rich diet, are essential for managing conditions like hypokalemia and hypertension, particularly in pregnant women. These dietary interventions can help mitigate the risks associated with electrolyte imbalances, which are critical for maintaining overall health during pregnancy. The relationship between diet and health outcomes highlights the importance of tailored nutritional guidance for mothers to support their health and that of their fetuses [Data: Entities (11386, 5544); Relationships (13120, 10604)].\"\r\n622,\"# Phosphorus and Related Health Conditions\n\nThe community focuses on the essential mineral phosphorus (Fósforo) and its critical role in various health conditions, particularly in relation to bone health, dietary needs, and specific medical conditions such as hypophosphatemia and oncogenic osteomalacia. The entities are interconnected through their relationships with phosphorus, dietary management, and the physiological implications of phosphorus levels in the body.\n\n## Fósforo's essential role in health\n\nFósforo is a vital mineral that plays a crucial role in various biological functions, including bone formation, energy production, and overall metabolism. It is particularly important in dietary recommendations for children and is included in parenteral nutrition, where its levels must be adjusted based on individual patient needs. The significance of phosphorus in health is underscored by its necessity for proper bone health and cellular function, making it a critical component in nutritional plans. [Data: Entities (1967); Relationships (4682, 8025)]\n\n## Impact of hypophosphatemia\n\nHypophosphatemia, characterized by low phosphorus levels in the blood, can arise from inadequate intake or specific medical conditions. This condition is particularly concerning in newborns and patients on parenteral nutrition, necessitating careful management to prevent complications. The relationship between phosphorus levels and hypophosphatemia highlights the importance of monitoring and adjusting phosphorus intake in vulnerable populations. [Data: Entities (2739); Relationships (2424, 8013)]\n\n## Interconnection with vitamin D and calcium\n\nPhosphorus levels are closely related to vitamin D and calcium, both of which are essential for maintaining bone health. Vitamin D facilitates the absorption of phosphorus in the intestines, while excessive phosphorus intake can negatively affect calcium absorption. This interconnectedness emphasizes the need for a balanced intake of these minerals to support overall bone health and prevent complications, particularly in pediatric patients. [Data: Entities (5617, 11519); Relationships (8011, 8015)]\n\n## Oncogenic osteomalacia and its causes\n\nOncogenic osteomalacia is a rare paraneoplastic syndrome characterized by biochemical abnormalities and bone mineralization issues similar to hypophosphatemic rickets. It is associated with mesenchymal tumors that secrete FGF23, a protein that regulates phosphorus metabolism. Understanding the relationship between these tumors and phosphorus levels is crucial for diagnosing and managing this condition effectively. [Data: Entities (5721, 5722, 5723); Relationships (15134, 15133)]\n\n## Dietary management of phosphorus\n\nDietary management of phosphorus is critical, especially for patients with chronic kidney disease (CKD) and those on specific diets like the ketogenic diet. High phosphorus levels can lead to significant health complications in CKD patients, necessitating careful monitoring and regulation of phosphorus intake. This highlights the importance of dietary guidance in managing phosphorus levels to ensure optimal health outcomes. [Data: Entities (11517, 11518); Relationships (8020, 8017)]\"\r\n\n\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n2470,NIÑOS,\"\"\"NIÑOS\"\" refers to children aged 1-18 years, encompassing a critical demographic with specific nutritional needs essential for optimal growth and development. This group is particularly sensitive to energy restrictions and requires tailored dietary recommendations, especially during key developmental periods such as infancy and adolescence. \n\nChildren are the primary consumers of pediatric formulas, which are designed to meet their unique dietary requirements based on age and health status. They are also the main focus of pediatric nutrition, with particular attention given to their growth and nutritional needs. Adequate intake of essential nutrients, such as iodine and calcium, is crucial for their proper growth and development. \n\nIn terms of dietary recommendations, children are the target population for guidelines regarding vitamin D and calcium intake. They may experience specific health issues, such as growth hormone deficiency and central hypothyroidism due to hypopituitarism, and are at risk of malnutrition, necessitating specialized nutritional support to promote healthy growth and development. \n\nChildren with certain conditions, such as congenital saccharase-isomaltase deficiency, must avoid specific carbohydrates to prevent adverse symptoms, and their tolerance may improve with age. Additionally, children under 4 years old are particularly susceptible to food allergies, largely due to their developing immune systems, with a significant number affected by cow's milk protein allergy.\n\nThe nutritional needs of children vary according to their age, weight, and health status, making them a unique population that often requires parenteral nutrition. They are also vulnerable to malnutrition associated with inflammatory bowel disease (IBD), which can lead to delays in growth and sexual development. \n\nRecent studies have shown that children can benefit from ketogenic diets, particularly for the management of epilepsy, demonstrating a significant reduction in seizure frequency. However, they are also at risk for nutrient-drug interactions due to their still-developing detoxification systems. \n\nOverall, \"\"NIÑOS\"\" encompasses a diverse group of children whose dietary needs and health considerations are critical for their growth, development, and overall well-being.\",28\r\n4816,RECOMENDACIONES DIETÉTICAS,\"The entity \"\"RECOMENDACIONES DIETÉTICAS\"\" refers to dietary recommendations, which are guidelines established to ensure that individuals receive the appropriate amount of nutrients and energy in their diet. These recommendations are particularly important for children, as they help to guide nutrient intake during critical growth periods. Additionally, dietary recommendations are essential for patients with chronic kidney disease, as they provide specific guidelines to maintain nutritional status and overall health. Overall, these dietary guidelines serve to promote well-being and prevent nutritional deficiencies across different populations.\",5\r\n3726,ADULTOS,\"\"\"ADULTOS\"\" refers to adults, who are individuals that have reached maturity and possess different nutritional requirements compared to children and infants. In the context of dietary guidelines for managing diabetes, adults are included as they generally tolerate starch and glucose polymers; however, they should avoid these if symptoms persist on a sucrose-free diet. Adults over the age of 19 are specifically referenced in energy requirement calculations. Additionally, adults can experience health issues such as adrenal insufficiency due to hypopituitarism and may face complications like osteomalacia or osteoporosis, particularly those with inflammatory bowel disease (EII), which can arise from malnutrition and other related factors. To maintain metabolic health, adults are advised to follow a balanced diet that includes corn starch and other essential nutrients. Furthermore, while adults may benefit from a ketogenic diet, its effectiveness may diminish over time due to low adherence to the dietary regimen.\",9\r\n12270,ESTADO NUTRICIONAL,\"The \"\"ESTADO NUTRICIONAL\"\" refers to the overall health condition of an individual in relation to their dietary intake and the utilization of nutrients by the body. It encompasses the assessment of how well a person's nutritional needs are being met and how effectively their body absorbs and uses these nutrients. This concept is particularly significant in the context of patients with pancreatic diseases, where nutritional status plays a critical role in their overall health and management.\",2\r\n7800,NAS,\"The NAS, or National Academy of Sciences, is a private, nonprofit institution comprised of distinguished scholars dedicated to scientific and engineering research. Established to provide expert advice on various scientific and technical issues, the NAS plays a significant role in formulating dietary guidelines. In 2002, the NAS published dietary recommendations that include the definition of the Recommended Dietary Allowance (RDA) for carbohydrates. Additionally, the NAS proposes formulas for calculating estimated energy requirements tailored to different age groups, further contributing to the understanding of nutritional needs across the lifespan.\",10\r\n8989,DUODENO,\"The duodeno, or duodenum, is the first part of the small intestine, playing a crucial role in the digestive process. It is primarily responsible for the chemical digestion of food, aided by enzymes and bile. In addition to its digestive functions, the duodeno is significant for nutrient absorption, specifically calcium and copper. Furthermore, it is the site where the final digestion of carbohydrates occurs, highlighting its importance in the overall digestive system.\",4\r\n5012,OSTEOMALACIA,\"OSTEOMALACIA is a condition characterized by the softening of bones, primarily due to a prolonged deficiency of vitamin D, which affects calcium absorption and leads to weakened bones. This condition can manifest in various contexts, including in patients with Wilson's disease and those receiving home parenteral nutrition. Osteomalacia results in symptoms such as bone pain and overall weakness, and it involves the deterioration of bone matrix mineralization, contributing to the fragility of the skeletal structure.\",7\r\n13341,AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY,\"The American Cancer Society is a nationwide voluntary health organization committed to eliminating cancer and enhancing the quality of life for individuals affected by the disease. In addition to its overarching mission, the organization offers specific guidelines regarding the nutritional needs of cancer patients, advising the use of multivitamins during chemotherapy and radiotherapy to support their health during treatment.\",3\r\n5729,1Α-HIDROXILASA,\"1α-hidroxilasa is an enzyme crucial for the activation of vitamin D, affecting calcium and phosphate metabolism\",2\r\n14200,INTERACCIÓN FARMACO-NUTRIENTE,La interacción fármaco-nutriente se refiere a cómo los fármacos y los nutrientes pueden influenciarse mutuamente en su eficacia y absorción.,4\r\n3213,DEFICIENCIA DE VITAMINA D,\"La deficiencia de vitamina D es una condición que puede provocar hipocalcemia y está asociada con una serie de problemas de salud. Esta deficiencia puede resultar en un aumento de la hormona paratiroidea (PTH) y está relacionada con un mayor riesgo de fracturas y otras enfermedades. Además, se ha vinculado a un deterioro cognitivo y puede aumentar el riesgo de demencia. En conjunto, estos efectos destacan la importancia de mantener niveles adecuados de vitamina D para la salud general y el bienestar.\",3\